<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ListView xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY - a comment ABOVE the root
        breaks `sf` deploy at conversion with a misleading "unable to find matching parent
        xml file" error.

        WS6/WS7 CORRECTION (2026-08-30). Two changes, both deliberate:

        1) COLUMNS re-ordered onto the standard six-column set now shared by all five Lead
           list views (New/Under Review/Qualified/Dead Leads/Review Queue): Deal Name,
           Status, Channel (LeadSource), Extraction Score, Broker, Age. LEAD.LAST_NAME /
           LEAD.FIRST_NAME / LEAD.COMPANY are dropped from the lead position - Deal_Name__c
           (a Property-centric, never-blank formula) replaces them, since Lead.Name is the
           BROKER's personal name, not the deal. Property_Address__c, Guidance_Price__c and
           Parse_Confidence__c are dropped as DISPLAY columns to match the shared six-column
           set exactly; Parse_Confidence__c remains load-bearing in the FILTER below.

        2) FILTER widened, GATE D (WS7). The filter was Parse_Confidence__c = LOW alone.
           Field_Confidence_JSON__c (a per-field confidence map) cannot itself be used in a
           list-view filter - Low_Confidence_Field_Count__c is the derived, filterable count
           built for exactly this. The new filter is
              Parse_Confidence__c = LOW  OR  Low_Confidence_Field_Count__c > 0
           via <booleanFilter>1 OR 2</booleanFilter>. THE OR IS LOAD BEARING - it JOINS the
           existing signal, it does NOT replace it. The two answer different questions:
           Parse_Confidence__c is a single whole-email band over is_acquisition_related;
           Low_Confidence_Field_Count__c counts individually weak DEAL fields inside an
           email that can otherwise be confidently classified. Replacing filter 1 with the
           new field would silently narrow this already-live queue - filter 1 is unchanged
           in isolation (byte-identical value), filter 2 only adds rows.

        3) 🔴 C2 FIX (2026-08-30, BA Gap-Closure code-review pass). At the time filter 1 was
           added above, Lead.Parse_Confidence__c had ZERO FieldPermissions rows on
           DPEG_Admin_Access or Broker_Protection_Access - the field carried an existing,
           deliberate "do not grant" note on Broker_Protection_Access written BEFORE it became
           a filter term here. Resolved by GRANTING read on both sets (the cheap, safe option)
           rather than assuming Salesforce degrades gracefully on an inaccessible filter field -
           that behaviour was never proven here and was not worth staking this queue on. See
           each set's own in-file note for the corrected reasoning. Low_Confidence_Field_Count__c
           (filter 2) was already granted read on both sets when this filter was written, so it
           needed no further action.
    -->
    <booleanFilter>1 OR 2</booleanFilter>
    <fullName>Review_Queue</fullName>
    <columns>Deal_Name__c</columns>
    <columns>LEAD.STATUS</columns>
    <columns>LEAD.LEAD_SOURCE</columns>
    <columns>Extraction_Score_Pct__c</columns>
    <columns>Broker_First__c</columns>
    <columns>Days_in_System__c</columns>
    <filterScope>Everything</filterScope>
    <filters>
        <field>Parse_Confidence__c</field>
        <operation>equals</operation>
        <value>LOW</value>
    </filters>
    <filters>
        <field>Low_Confidence_Field_Count__c</field>
        <operation>greaterThan</operation>
        <value>0</value>
    </filters>
    <label>Review Queue</label>
</ListView>
